# Live database — the source of truth for all kanji/user data, NOT a rebuildable
# cache. Excluded from git only because it's a binary blob; back it up separately
# (see the kanji-db-backup systemd timer) before ever touching it by hand.
backend/kanji.db
# SQLite WAL sidecars — regenerated whenever the DB is opened, and committed by
# accident on 2026-09-10 by a `git add -A` while a dev server held the DB open.
backend/kanji.db-shm
backend/kanji.db-wal
backend/backups/

# User-uploaded images (glyph-less primitives). backup_db.py snapshots these
# alongside kanji.db; offsite_backup.py copies both artifacts off-host.
backend/uploads/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Node
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# PDF books — large binaries, not versioned
*.pdf

# Misc
preview?*
*.DS_Store
.env

# audit_decomposition.py working files — LLM audit cache + generated report
audit_results.jsonl
audit_report.md

# cjkvi-ids' ids.txt — third-party upstream data every audit script reads
# (curled fresh each session per the search-quality-audit task brief's step 0,
# e.g. `curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cjkvi/cjkvi-ids/master/ids.txt
# -o backend/ids.txt`), not this project's own data. Was never gitignored
# before, which a stop-hook's generic "untracked files" check flagged.
backend/ids.txt
backend/decomposition_history.json
